            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your 49-year-old female patient, admitted on 15/06/2020 with confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection. On admission, she presented with fever, dyspnoea, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray and CT thorax confirmed bilateral COVID-19 pneumonia. Blood tests including inflammatory markers, arterial blood gases, and full blood count were performed. She was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, dexamethasone, and anticoagulation. Vital signs and pulse oximetry were monitored continuously. Respiratory physiotherapy was initiated to support recovery. The patient showed satisfactory clinical improvement and was discharged on 17/06/2020 in a recovering condition. Please ensure outpatient follow-up within two weeks, including repeat chest imaging if clinically indicated. Isolation and hygiene measures were discussed with the patient prior to discharge.</div>"
            },
